; POLYGON (0.8.1-PT36, #934): directions with cardinalSinCos (REGOLE-NUMERICHE.md, section 2,
; point 1; D8): the vertices of a square inscribed with the radius given by a point on an axis are
; quarter turns, hence exact, and the absolute tolerance is 0. The first vertex is the point, then
; counterclockwise (card, point 2). The second POLYGON takes the proposals 4 and I with Enter.
!tolerance absolute 0
POLYGON
4
0,0
I
10,0
POLYGON

100,0

100,10
